<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuelan M-2 rises 1.0 pct in week to Sept 6.</title>
<headline>Venezuelan M-2 rises 1.0 pct in week to Sept 6.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan money supply, as measured by the monetary aggregate M-2, rose 1.00 percent, or 43 billion bolivars to 4.339 trillion bolivars in the week to Sept 6, the central bank said.</p>
<p>At the beginning of 1996, M-2 was 3.530 trillion bolivars.</p>
<p>The monetary base, meanwhile, slipped 0.81 percent, or 9 billion bolivars, to 1.068 trillion in the week to Sept 6.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600.</p>
</text>
